title: "Generalized Structural Trigger and Computational Growth Intelligence"

version: "1.0.0"

date-released: "2026-09-15"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Tan"
    given-names: "Sizhe"

abstract: >-
  Generalized Structural Trigger and Computational Growth Intelligence
  (GST-CGI) presents a structural-intelligence framework that extends
  Two-Way CCC beyond String-DNA-only trigger representations toward
  generalized structural triggers with explicit structural state,
  comparison semantics, controlled behavior, evidence APIs, and
  policy perspectives. The framework introduces the Leaf Resolution
  Gate with DECIDE, REFINE, LEFTOVER, and DELEGATE outcomes; treats
  Leftover as a first-class structural boundary and input to Delta
  Intelligence; introduces the Leaf Sandbox Package and Delegated
  Structural Unfolding for policy-bounded external computation; and
  develops Computational Growth Intelligence as the capability to
  construct, refine, validate, delegate, compose, and govern the
  computational structures through which future intelligence is
  performed. The framework further distinguishes Experience Growth,
  Performance Growth, Computational-Structure Growth, and
  Computational-System Growth, and extends these ideas toward
  policy-governed AI computational ecosystems.

